---
description: Styling — CSS modules, tokens, no inline styles
globs: src/**/*.{ts,tsx,css}
alwaysApply: true
---

# Styles

- No inline `style={...}` in JSX. Styles go through CSS modules only.
- CSS file name is `styles.module.css` (plural). Never `style.module.css`.
- Prefer `.root` as the outer wrapper class (match Header / PageShell).
- 2-space indent in CSS, same as TS.
- Do not invent HEX when an Ant Design token or a variable from `src/ui/theme/` / `src/ui/colors/` already covers it. HEX only when no token fits.
- Do not restate default typography. Base font-size / line-height inherit from the theme.
- Set `font-size` / `line-height` in `.module.css` only when the value differs from the default — then use theme tokens (`--font-size-*`, `--line-height-*`), not hard-coded pixels.
- If design changes a base size, update the token once in `src/ui/theme/fonts.css`; do not patch dozens of CSS files.
